<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Tinos and Mykonos</h1><p class="st-meta">1207 CE – 1390 CE · capital Tinos</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Island lordship of the Venetian Ghisi family in the Cyclades, which ended when the last Ghisi bequeathed Tinos and Mykonos to Venice in 1390.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The brothers Andrea and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geremia-ghisi">Geremia Ghisi</a>, Venetian nobles, conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tinos">Tinos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykonos">Mykonos</a> around 1207 in the wave of private Venetian ventures that followed the Fourth Crusade. They also acquired other small islands, including parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-sporades">Northern Sporades</a>, and recognised the suzerainty of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/latin-empire">Latin Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Ghisi held the islands as a hereditary family domain, ruling from the hilltop castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/exobourgo">Exobourgo</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tinos">Tinos</a> over Greek farmers and fishermen, and were drawn into the feudal politics of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/triarchy-of-negroponte">Triarchy of Negroponte</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-achaea">Principality of Achaea</a>. Byzantine raids under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licario">Licario</a> in the 1270s cost them some islands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Turkish raids grew in the 14th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giorgio-iii-ghisi">Giorgio III Ghisi</a>, the last of the line, died in 1390 and left his islands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tinos">Tinos</a> until 1715 as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/venetian-tinos">Venetian Tinos</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1207 CE – 1390 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.72%;width:3.64%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1207 CE – 1390 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tinos</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Andrea Ghisi, Geremia Ghisi, Giorgio III Ghisi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity (rulers), Eastern Orthodox Christianity (population)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Italian, Medieval Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ghisi lordship</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=lordship-of-tinos-and-mykonos" aria-label="Lordship of Tinos and Mykonos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5309 827 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Lordship of Tinos and Mykonos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5629 1083L5636 1097M5629 1083L5629 1083"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5636 1097h0M5629 1083h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5629 1083h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5629 1083h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tinos. <a href="/atlas?year=1298&amp;focus=lordship-of-tinos-and-mykonos">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
